<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tortor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		torqueo, I. B. 2., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an executioner</i>, <i>tormentor</i>,
				<i>torturer.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum jam tortor, atque essent tormenta ipsa
					defessa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Clu. 63, 177</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Phil. 11, 3, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin.
				4, 12, 31</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 14, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 3,
				5, 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 14, 21</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>He that brandishes</i>, <i>handles.</i> Balearis habenae, <i><span class="en">Luc. 3,
			710</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tortor</span></b> ,
			ōris, <i>an epithet of
			Apollo</i>, <i>as the flayer of Marsyas</i>, under
			which name he was worshipped in a part of Rome, <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 70</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occultum quatiente animo tortore flagellum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 195</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
